Description: An R implementation of the Grouping-Scoring-Modeling (G-S-M)
    framework for data analysis with prior knowledge. Groups features based
    on external knowledge sources (e.g. disease associations, pathways,
    gene ontology), scores groups using machine learning classifiers, and
    builds predictive models from top-ranked groups. Supports Monte Carlo
    cross-validation with pluggable backends for pre-scoring, scoring, and
    modeling steps.
